<!--
  The month grid, for the 24dp status-bar slot: nine cells on a squircle, and today is the one
  that is round.

  Shape is the only thing available here — the system keeps the alpha channel and throws the
  colour away — so the day the launcher icon marks in amber is marked by being a circle instead.
  It is the same size as its neighbours on purpose: a bigger dot reads as "more important", a
  round one reads as "this one".

  Both the ground and the eight ordinary cells are superellipses (|x|^5 + |y|^5 = 1) rather than
  rounded rectangles. That is what keeps the flat-sided squares distinct from the circle at the
  size this is actually seen; a generous corner radius makes them read as circles too and the
  distinction disappears.

  Even-odd, and never more than two shapes deep: the ground, and one cell punched through it.

  No android:tint — the system tints a notification's small icon itself.
-->
